{"id": "c5cde6a7-75fa-4dd3-847d-76fad002500b", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll look into the orders-web CloudFormation stack to pull together what we can for the scoping sheet. Business-judgment columns (customer-retained criticality, target availability %, customer comments) will need the business owners either way — but I can populate the technical columns from what's actually deployed.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_xjx2PDppt3VsrsPHJEEEGk", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Locate the CloudFormation stack named 'orders-web' in eu-west-1, identify which AWS account it lives in, and build a resource/architecture profile for a DR scoping sheet.",
  "context": "Ops team is filling in a disaster-recovery scoping sheet for the 'orders website' app. Need to populate as many columns as possible from actual account data: Application code/name, observed tag names, AWS account ID, list of resources in the stack, any 'availability' tag (24/7 vs business hours) on resources, any criticality/code-label/parent-business-application tags, whether resources are Multi-AZ (for RTO/RPO on loss of an AZ), what the recovery architecture looks like (active-active/hot standby/warm standby/pilot light/backup-restore) based on what's actually deployed (e.g. ASG min capacity across AZs, RDS Multi-AZ, read replicas, EKS pods spread across AZs), backup/snapshot retention settings (for restore-time-from-backup), and whether any part of the stack runs on EKS (and if so, which namespace/labels point to it).",
  "resources": ["CloudFormation stack: orders-web", "region: eu-west-1"],
  "timeframe": "current state as of now",
  "criteria": "1) Find the stack via CloudFormation (list_stacks/describe_stacks/list_stack_resources) across available accounts associated with this agent space. 2) Report the account ID it's in. 3) List all stack resources with type, name, and tags. 4) Identify any tags indicating application code, business application name, criticality, or availability window. 5) Inspect key resources (ASG/EC2, RDS/Aurora, ALB, EKS, S3, DynamoDB, etc.) for Multi-AZ configuration, backup/snapshot retention period, and automated backup settings. 6) If any resource references an EKS cluster, identify the cluster name and look for a namespace associated with this stack (via tags/labels) — note cluster name and candidate namespace so I can confirm via kubectl myself if needed. 7) Return findings as a structured list keyed by resource, not a narrative."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Find CloudFormation stack orders-web in eu-west-1 and its resources/tags"}], "created_at": null}
